    "updated_at": "2019-02-26T14:05:37Z",
    "body": "That's a fair point. Maybe we could use \"is a `Text` object\" for IDL values, and use \"implements\" for JS values? I think using \"corresponding ECMAScript value\" would generally be a sign of bad layering; in the few cases that need it, I'd consider using https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#interface-to-es.",
